## Your CI

<%#hasCi%>
Your existing CI was left alone. It does not know about the baseline, so add a job that does:
<%/hasCi%>
<%^hasCi%>
No CI was found. If you add one, this is the job:
<%/hasCi%>

```yaml
name: sdlc-verify
on: [pull_request]
jobs:
  verify:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      # install the toolchains this project needs here, exactly as your other workflows do
      - run: ./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc setup
      - run: ./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc verify
```

(Workflows are protected from agents by design; a human adds this one.)

## Configure

| What | Where |
|---|---|
| Add, drop or change a gate | `gates` in `.ai/sdlc.json` (`id`, `stage`, `cwd`, `cmd`, `required`, `timeoutSeconds`) |
| Which AI tool | `./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc agent` lists them (installed or not) and saves your choice in `.ai/agent.local.json` (not committed) |
| Make skips fatal | `facts.strictSkips: true` |
| Loop budget | `loop.maxIterations`, `loop.noProgressLimit` |
| Re-detect after changing the repository | run `scaffolder adopt` again: it adds files that are missing and never overwrites yours (`--force` overwrites the generated ones) |
